            0.169,
            0.136,
            0.828,
            0.239
          ],
          "content": "(ix) 1, 3, 9, 27, . . . (x) $a , 2 a , 3 a , 4 a , \\cdots$ (xi) $a , a ^ { 2 } , a ^ { 3 } , a ^ { 4 } , \\ldots$ (xii) $\\left[ \\sqrt{2} , \\sqrt{8} , \\sqrt{18} , \\sqrt{32} , \\cdots \\right.$ (xiii) $\\left[ \\sqrt{3} , \\sqrt{6} , \\sqrt{9} , \\sqrt{12} , \\cdots \\right]$ (xiv) $1 ^ { 2 } , 3 ^ { 2 } , 5 ^ { 2 } , 7 ^ { 2 } , \\ldots$ (xv) $1 ^ { 2 } , 5 ^ { 2 } , 7 ^ { 2 } , 7 3 , \\ldots$"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.257,
            0.346,
            0.277
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "5.3 nth Term of an AP"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.284,
            0.902,
            0.362
          ],
          "content": "Let us consider the situation again, given in Section 5.1 in which Reena applied for a job and got selected. She has been offered the job with a starting monthly salary of \\` 8000, with an annual increment of \\` 500. What would be her monthly salary for the fifth year?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.367,
            0.901,
            0.406
          ],
          "content": "To answer this, let us first see what her monthly salary for the second year would be."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.411,
            0.9,
            0.458
          ],
          "content": "It would be $8000+500=8500$ In the same way, we can find the monthly salary for the 3rd, 4th and 5th year by adding \\` 500 to the salary of the previous year. Se the"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.451,
            0.899,
            0.565
          ],
          "content": "o, the salary for the 3rd $\\begin{aligned} year  &= \\mp (8500 + 500) \\\\&= \\mp (8000 + 500 + 500) \\\\&= \\mp (8000 + 2 \\times 500) \\\\&= \\mp (8000 + (3 - 1) \\times 500) \\\\&= \\mp 9000 \\\\&= \\mp 9000 \\quad \\cdots \\quad \\cdots \\quad \\cdots\\end{aligned}$ (for the **3rd year**)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.567,
            0.901,
            0.682
          ],
          "content": "Salary for the 4th year $\\begin{aligned}&= \\vec{ 飞 } \\left( 9000 + 500 \\right) \\\\&= \\vec{ 飞 } \\left( 8000 + 500 + 500 + 500 \\right) \\\\&= \\vec{ 飞 } \\left( 8000 + 3 \\times 500 \\right) \\\\&= \\vec{ 飞 } \\left[ 8000 + \\left( \\mathbf{4} - \\mathbf{1} \\right) \\times 500 \\right] \\\\&= \\vec{ 飞 } 9500\\end{aligned}$ (for the **4th year**)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.687,
            0.9,
            0.813
          ],
          "content": "Salary for the 5th year = \\` (9500 + 500) = \\` (8000+500+500+500 + 500) = \\` (8000 + 4 × 500) = \\` [8000 + **(5 – 1)** × 500] (for the **5th year**) = \\` 10000"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.822,
            0.605,
            0.869
          ],
          "content": "Observe that we are getting a list of numbers 8000, 8500, 9000, 9500, 10000, . . ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.877,
            0.482,
            0.897
          ],
          "content": "These numbers are in AP. (Why?)"
        },
        {
